butesThis group of attributes includes index information, and can have different values for each family.Type attributesThis group of attributes includes performance data attributes of a familyTable gives an overview on the structure of header information fields in a CSV file.Overview on the Structure of Header InformationSection NameField NameDescriptionTypeFamily-Name of the performance data familyStringVersion-Software version of the NEStringAttributeNE_IDNE identifier given by the operatorStringSYSTEM_IDNE numeric ID given by the EMSIntegerNE_NAMENE name given by the operatorStringINIT_TIMEDate and time when performance data collection started (format: YYYY-mm-DD hh:24mm:ss)Time StampTIME_OFFSETTimeOffset when performance data collection startedStringGRAN_PERIODGranularity period (5 minutes )IntegerLOCATIONPerformance IndexsStringTYPE#nTypes of a familyString2.5.1.1.2.3 Content DataContent data shows the values corresponding to the attribute field names in the header information. This section presents the values of the NEs managed by the EMS. Values are separated by commas. When a value is absent, then no value and no space is presented between the commas. File content follow#family:Resource#version:20.A.0#index:ShelfId/SlotId#attribute:NE_ID,SYSTEM_ID,NE_NAME,INIT_TIME,TIME_OFFSET,GRAN_PERIOD,LOCATION,MemUsageAvg(%),MemUsageMin(%),MemUsageMax(%),MemUsageTot(%),MemUsageCnt(count),CpuUsageAvg(%),CpuUsageMin(%),CpuUsageMax(%),CpuUsageMaxDuration(s),CpuUsageTot(%),CpuUsageCnt(count),DiskUsageAvg(%),DiskUsageMin(%),DiskUsageMax(%),DiskUsageTot(%),DiskUsageCnt(count)eNB_11043,11043,ENB_11043,2020-01-30 08:45:00,,5,ShelfId0/SlotId0,38.81,38.76,38.87,3492.52,90.00,7.02,7.00,8.00,20.00,632.00,90.00,8.97,8.96,8.99,807.73,90.00EMS Performance DataUSM generate USM performance data files every 1 hour. These performance data files contain the follow